DeepSeek Desktop Shell

This is an unofficial, community-built desktop wrapper. It is not produced,
endorsed, sponsored, or supported by DeepSeek (深度求索).

The software contains no DeepSeek code, models, or assets. It loads the public
website https://chat.deepseek.com/ in an embedded Chromium window, exactly as a
browser would. All content, trademarks, and services shown inside the window
belong to their respective owners and remain subject to DeepSeek's own terms of
service.

The application icon is derived (background keyed out, resized) from the mark
served by chat.deepseek.com itself at
https://fe-static.deepseek.com/chat/icon-512.png. The whale logo and the
"DeepSeek" name are trademarks of their owner. They are used here only to
identify which service the window displays, and this project claims no rights
over them.

The name "DeepSeek" is used only to describe what website the shell displays.
No affiliation is claimed or implied.

## The opt-in agent

The optional agent (off by default) automates the website the way a person would:
it types into the composer and reads the answer back. It does not call an API, does
not proxy traffic, and does not modify the page. Even so:

- using automation against the service may breach DeepSeek's terms of use, and the
  account used with it may be rate-limited or restricted. The risk sits with whoever
  turns the feature on, and the app warns about it before enabling it;
- the agent executes model-generated file operations and shell commands on the local
  machine. Review what it does. The authors accept no liability for damage caused by
  generated code.
